1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:02,417
Refund Office turns a missing item into

2
00:00:02,417 --> 00:00:03,900
an inspectable decision.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,638
The agent investigates.

4
00:00:06,887 --> 00:00:09,041
A person controls every refund.

5
00:00:09,418 --> 00:00:11,767
The paperwork has entered its dramatic era.

6
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:14,193
Welcome to the office.

7
00:00:15,523 --> 00:00:17,543
A customer reports a missing travel mug

8
00:00:17,543 --> 00:00:19,115
from a sixty pound order.

9
00:00:19,784 --> 00:00:22,435
A convincing complaint is a starting point.

10
00:00:23,105 --> 00:00:25,392
The office still needs evidence before recommending

11
00:00:25,392 --> 00:00:26,533
any refund.

12
00:00:30,523 --> 00:00:32,182
Reception opens the case.

13
00:00:32,427 --> 00:00:34,804
Evidence checks the order and packing record.

14
00:00:35,345 --> 00:00:38,058
The analyser uses local rules and synthetic

15
00:00:38,058 --> 00:00:38,737
data.

16
00:00:39,393 --> 00:00:42,271
These desks represent stages of one workflow,

17
00:00:42,323 --> 00:00:44,050
rather than separate agents.

18
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:47,416
The packing record shows two of three

19
00:00:47,416 --> 00:00:48,522
items supplied.

20
00:00:48,983 --> 00:00:51,053
The missing mug costs twenty pounds.

21
00:00:51,305 --> 00:00:53,906
That supports a twenty pound proposal, attached

22
00:00:53,906 --> 00:00:56,007
to the item, its price and the

23
00:00:56,007 --> 00:00:57,230
supporting records.

24
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:01,735
Next comes policy.

25
00:01:02,127 --> 00:01:05,126
The service checks evidence, exact amount, remaining

26
00:01:05,126 --> 00:01:08,060
balance, previous remedies and the refund limit.

27
00:01:08,636 --> 00:01:10,929
Passing these checks makes a proposal eligible

28
00:01:10,929 --> 00:01:13,484
for review; it does not authorise payment.

29
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:17,184
This is the deliberate pause.

30
00:01:17,534 --> 00:01:19,722
Every new refund waits for a person.

31
00:01:20,477 --> 00:01:22,631
The review screen shows the exact amount,

32
00:01:22,697 --> 00:01:25,027
order, item and policy version.

33
00:01:25,453 --> 00:01:27,203
You can open the evidence before deciding

34
00:01:27,203 --> 00:01:28,417
whether to approve.

35
00:01:30,542 --> 00:01:33,529
For this isolated demonstration, the reviewer approved

36
00:01:33,529 --> 00:01:35,832
twenty pounds and recorded a reason.

37
00:01:36,569 --> 00:01:38,658
That decision belongs to these facts.

38
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:41,910
Change the evidence, amount or policy, and

39
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:43,783
the old approval cannot carry the refund

40
00:01:43,783 --> 00:01:44,256
through.

41
00:01:45,521 --> 00:01:47,760
Only after approval does the saved operation

42
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,547
proceed.

43
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:51,334
The demonstration produces a local receipt linked

44
00:01:51,334 --> 00:01:52,547
to the approved amount.

45
00:01:53,562 --> 00:01:54,880
This is a simulation:

46
00:01:55,208 --> 00:01:57,209
no real money moves, and no Stripe

47
00:01:57,209 --> 00:01:58,484
transaction is claimed.

48
00:02:00,535 --> 00:02:02,613
For a repeat request, the remedy register

49
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:04,447
finds the existing result for the same

50
00:02:04,447 --> 00:02:05,148
issue.

51
00:02:05,608 --> 00:02:08,248
The outcome is zero additional refund.

52
00:02:08,801 --> 00:02:11,030
A second investigation must not become a

53
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,195
second payment.

54
00:02:15,519 --> 00:02:16,996
Some cases should stop.

55
00:02:17,663 --> 00:02:19,394
Here, the delivery record conflicts with the

56
00:02:19,394 --> 00:02:20,467
customer report.

57
00:02:21,261 --> 00:02:22,630
The office holds the case.

58
00:02:22,932 --> 00:02:24,781
A person can request evidence or close

59
00:02:24,781 --> 00:02:25,697
it with a reason.

60
00:02:26,246 --> 00:02:28,519
Approval cannot erase conflicting evidence.

61
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:33,021
History keeps the complaint, evidence, checks and

62
00:02:33,021 --> 00:02:34,130
decisions together.

63
00:02:34,817 --> 00:02:37,086
A downloadable decision packet adds the operation

64
00:02:37,086 --> 00:02:38,004
and receipt.

65
00:02:38,468 --> 00:02:40,758
The local reviewer label identifies this demo's

66
00:02:40,758 --> 00:02:43,400
operator; it is not an authenticated production

67
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,085
identity.

68
00:02:45,519 --> 00:02:46,902
Autonomous preparation.

69
00:02:47,139 --> 00:02:48,744
Explicit human approval.

70
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:50,219
A traceable result.

71
00:02:50,514 --> 00:02:52,649
The miniature office makes the workflow visible.

72
00:02:53,088 --> 00:02:55,094
This prototype uses a local rule based

73
00:02:55,094 --> 00:02:58,174
analyser, synthetic records and simulated payments.

74
00:02:58,363 --> 00:02:59,572
You remain in charge.
